This gives us an explicit intuition organ

Imagine a decision represented by thousands of signals:

x=(x_1,x_2,\ldots,x_n)

The Intuition Organ produces a compact latent state:

z=f_\theta(x,\text{context},\text{memory},\text{body})

and then something extremely cheap:

I=(a,c,s)

where:

* a = recommended direction/action
* c = confidence
* s = salience/urgency

It might output:

LEAN: NO
CONFIDENCE: .72
URGENCY: .41
CAUSE: not yet decompressed

That last line matters.

Intuition doesn’t need to invent an explanation immediately.

Instead MBR can attempt to reacquire the latent causes.

Mother Duck fetches the lineage.

Prism decomposes the feeling.

Goal Seek asks which missing observation would distinguish the competing explanations.

Mirror checks whether the eventual explicit explanation actually reconstructs the intuitive signature.

So we avoid a classic failure:

intuition fires → conscious mind fabricates a story afterward.

The organ is allowed to say:

“signal detected; causal interpretation unresolved.”

That’s much cleaner.

